# Fre3nder licensing

Fre3nder uses path-specific licensing. The authoritative machine-readable
assignments are in `REUSE.toml`; complete license texts are in `LICENSES/`.

- Project-authored Fre3nder system material is licensed under
  `AGPL-3.0-or-later`.
- Project-authored material in `research/` is licensed under `MIT`, except
  where a specific assignment preserves an existing product-documentation
  license or identifies third-party/derived material. Preserved snapshots keep
  `AGPL-3.0-or-later`; mixed records identify their MIT/AGPL section boundaries.
- Third-party and derived material remains under its applicable license.

Repository revisions through
`bb22b9d915a2205d7d9b4b38adf436d512f4d8b7` were made available under the MIT
License. Those previously granted MIT permissions remain valid. See
`docs/licensing-and-provenance.md` for the transition and provenance policy.
